╭─ Stay up to date? ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Once a day, a moment after the prompt, Oh My Shell can ask GitHub which    │
│ release is the newest. That is one request for a release name.             │
│ Nothing is downloaded or installed, and you see one line when there is     │
│ news. `omsh update` installs it, and checks the file first.                │
│ You can change this later: Ctrl+P, Settings, update.check.                 │
│                                                                            │
│ [⟨4⟩Y⟨0⟩es, check daily]  ⟨7⟩ ⟨0⟩⟨4;7⟩N⟨0⟩⟨7⟩o, I'll run omsh update --check myself ⟨0⟩              │
╰─ ←→ ⟨2⟩move · ⟨0⟩Enter ⟨2⟩choose · ⟨0⟩Esc ⟨2⟩no⟨0⟩ ──────────────────────────────────────────╯
